WEBVTT

NOTE On-screen visual text only; this approved video has no audio track.

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:07.350
Ten services at ten euros each mean one hundred euros of spending.

2
00:00:07.350 --> 00:00:14.200
Twenty services of equal quality at five euros each also mean one hundred.

3
00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:22.617
At first-period prices, volume rises from one hundred to two hundred: distinguish nominal and real GDP.

4
00:00:23.117 --> 00:00:29.967
Cooking at home for one’s own consumption provides a service without a market transaction.

5
00:00:29.967 --> 00:00:36.817
Buying the equivalent service for fifty euros adds market production.

6
00:00:36.817 --> 00:00:44.867
That accounting boundary does not prove the earlier service had no value; household accounts complement GDP.

7
00:00:45.367 --> 00:00:52.217
Output of one hundred units across ten residents gives ten per person.

8
00:00:52.217 --> 00:00:59.067
Output rises to one hundred twenty while population reaches fifteen.

9
00:00:59.067 --> 00:01:06.417
That is now eight per person: read the aggregate together with its denominator.

10
00:01:06.917 --> 00:01:14.833
GDP of 100 minus 20 of fixed-capital consumption leaves net domestic product of 80.

11
00:01:14.833 --> 00:01:21.683
In another period, GDP of 105 minus 30 leaves net domestic product of 75.

12
00:01:21.683 --> 00:01:29.033
GDP is gross: it does not deduct fixed-capital consumption.

13
00:01:29.533 --> 00:01:36.383
The same one hundred units are produced in an eight-hour workday.

14
00:01:36.383 --> 00:01:43.233
An improvement preserves quantity and quality with six hours.

15
00:01:43.233 --> 00:01:50.583
The two freed hours can have value without becoming additional production.

16
00:01:51.083 --> 00:01:57.933
Assume one hundred identical services are worth fifteen euros each to their buyers.

17
00:01:57.933 --> 00:02:05.850
Price falls from ten to five with quantity unchanged; spending falls from one thousand to five hundred.

18
00:02:05.850 --> 00:02:14.650
Under that assumed valuation, buyer surplus rises from five hundred to one thousand; it is not total wellbeing.

